ds that occupy a portion of an app's layout. They stay on screen while user=
s are interacting with the app, either anchored at the top or bottom of the=
 screen or inline with content as the user scrolls. Banner ads can refresh =
automatically after a certain period of time.</p>

<p>Banner ads are effective because they work well with many types of apps =
and don=E2=80=99t take up much space. They=E2=80=99re also the simplest ad =
format to implement.</p>

<h2>Types of banner ads</h2>

<div class=3D"no-margin"></div>

<div class=3D"no-margin"><div class=3D"tip">
  <div class=3D"no-margin">Adaptive banners are the newest generation of ba=
nner ads and offer the best user experience. They=E2=80=99re intended to re=
place smart and standard banners.</div>
</div>
</div>

<table class=3D"nice-table wide">
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Type</strong></td>
      <td><strong>Description</strong></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Adaptive</td>
      <td>
      <p>There are two types of adaptive banners:</p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Anchored</strong> adaptive banners are expected to be a=
lways on-screen,&nbsp;locked to the screen=E2=80=99s top or bottom.</li>
        <li><strong>Inline</strong> adaptive banners are intended for place=
ment inside scrollable content and can be much larger as the user typically=
 scrolls past them.</li>
      </ul>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Standard</td>
      <td>Fits only the specified banner size (<a href=3D"https://developer=
s.google.com/admob/android/banner#banner_sizes" rel=3D"noopener" target=3D"=
_blank">Android</a>and&nbsp;<a href=3D"https://developers.google.com/admob/=
ios/banner#banner_sizes" rel=3D"noopener" target=3D"_blank">iOS</a>). Only =
ads that fit the specified size can be served.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Smart (deprecated)</td>
      <td>Fills screen width on any device using a fixed height. This means=
 the ad may appear small on some devices.&nbsp;
      <div class=3D"note">
        <div class=3D"no-margin"><strong>Note</strong>: Support for smart b=
anners is deprecated. Consider implementing adaptive banners as a replaceme=
nt for smart banners.&nbsp;</div>
      </div>
      </td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>About adaptive banners</h2>

<p>Adaptive banners consider the device in use, the ad width you=E2=80=99ve=
 specified, and the aspect ratios of all available demand. They dynamically=
 adjust the ad size for a variety of devices and screen sizes without exces=
sive custom code.</p>

<p>Adaptive banners aim to fill the entire ad slot size, but will select cr=
eatives for maximum performance. This means that ad creatives may fit edge =
to edge or be centered in the ad slot, depending on which advertiser bids h=
ighest for that impression.</p>

<div class=3D"note"><strong>Note</strong>: Adaptive banners don=E2=80=99t s=
tretch, crop, or modify advertiser creatives.</div>

<p>You can implement two types of adaptive banners: anchored and inline ada=
ptive banners.</p>

<h3>Anchored adaptive banners</h3>

<p>Anchored adaptive banners have a relatively small maximum height to avoi=
d taking up too much of the screen; they have a maximum height of 150x150dp=
 (Android) or 150x150pts (iOS) or 20% of the device height in the chosen or=
ientation, whichever is smaller. Anchored to the top or bottom of the scree=
n, anchored adaptive banners set an optimal ad slot size for any device. On=
ce set, the anchored adaptive banner slot size doesn't change.</p>

<h4>Collapsible banners (Beta)</h4>

<p>You can also add a parameter to your anchored adaptive banners to make i=
t a&nbsp;<a href=3D"https://support.google.com/admob/answer/14160679" rel=
=3D"noopener">collapsible banner ad</a>. Collapsible banners initially show=
 the selected banner as a larger overlay with an option to collapse the exp=
anded banner to a standard banner size. This offers more room to convey the=
 advertiser=E2=80=99s message, which provides better visibility and higher =
click-through rates.</p>

<div class=3D"tip">
  <div class=3D"no-margin">Learn more about implementing anchored adaptive =
banners for <a href=3D"https://developers.google.com/admob/android/banner/c=
ollapsible" rel=3D"noopener" target=3D"_blank">Android</a>, <a href=3D"http=
s://developers.google.com/admob/ios/banner/collapsible" rel=3D"noopener" ta=
rget=3D"_blank">iOS</a> and <a href=3D"https://developers.google.com/admob/=
unity/banner/collapsible" rel=3D"noopener" target=3D"_blank">Unity</a>.</di=
v>
</div>

<h3>Inline adaptive banners</h3>

<p data-outlined=3D"false" class=3D"">Inline adaptive banners are shown in =
scrollable content, the slot height reserved for advertiser creatives may c=
hange from one page-view to the next. This helps maximize eligible advertis=
er demand and improve revenue performance. Inline adaptive banners don=E2=
=80=99t have hard size limits. While APIs are available for publishers to s=
et their own limits on height for inline adaptive banners, such limits may =
reduce performance.</p>

<div class=3D"tip">
  <div class=3D"no-margin" data-outlined=3D"false">Learn more about impleme=
nting adaptive inline banners for <a href=3D"https://developers.google.com/=
admob/android/banner/inline-adaptive" rel=3D"noopener" target=3D"_blank">An=
droid</a> and <a href=3D"https://developers.google.com/admob/ios/banner/inl=
ine-adaptive" rel=3D"noopener" target=3D"_blank">iOS</a>.</div>
</div>

